alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure doc "The png_oracle entry, with two commands; every path is relative to the working directory. `png_oracle check LIST DIR` reads LIST, whose lines are `valid NAME` or `invalid NAME`, and decodes DIR/NAME.png with decode_png for each. An invalid case passes when decoding fails. A valid case passes when decoding succeeds with the width and height of the little-endian u32 pair that starts DIR/NAME.rgba, width * height * 4 pixel bytes, and every pixel byte equal to the rest of that file. It prints up to 10 failures as `NAME: reason`, then the summary line `png: C cases, P passed, F failed`, and exits with 0 exactly when LIST holds at least one case and every case passes, 1 when a case fails, and 2 when LIST or DIR cannot be read. DIR is opened one component at a time with std::fs::open_directory, which refuses a symbolic link, so no component of DIR may be one. `png_oracle time REPEAT FILE...` reads each FILE once and then decodes it REPEAT times, summing every 4093rd pixel byte of each decoded image as tests/png/reference.c does, and prints `checksum N`; it exits with 1 when a decode fails and 2 when a FILE cannot be read.";
